cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the audit results, please cite it as below."
title: "Enzyme Condition Audit: missing assay conditions and hidden variant data in public enzyme kinetics datasets"
abstract: >-
  A quantified audit of EnzyExtractDB (176,463 records) showing 0.0% coverage
  of the 'solution' (buffer) field and no fields at all for ionic strength,
  expression host, or substrate concentration - while 90% of papers do report
  buffer compositions. Also documents that ~13x more variant-level data is
  compressed into list columns than is exposed as rows in public enzyme
  datasets. Includes a condition-completer prototype (LLM extraction +
  deterministic ionic-strength computation) and a gold-standard evaluation
  (pH recall 98.0%, temperature 97.3%).
type: software
